      "text": "I've seen documentaries on all these places in-details, except Lagos Nigeria - Probably due to the amount of scam coming from Lagos, targeting elder;y Americans,(stealing their life savings). I feel badly for ALL ppl living like this. Unfortunately, I know SOOO many Americans, also just 1 paycheck away from homelessness. We NEED to focus on fixing our country's, (US) affordable housing CRISIS, so we can be in a position to help others, again..The need is real, the desperation is real.Many ppl like to blame mismanaged finances, but the real problem is that someone can work 2 full-time jobs, & still be unable to afford basic housing - the minimum wage & housing price inflation gap continues to rise - more & more ppl can't be approved nor afford a small basic apartment in the US anymore. I've been paying $3k/mo. for a studio the last few yrs. - My rent started @ 2k/mo. & rose by 1k over the last 2 yrs. w/ no updates or added amenities...prices just keep rising & rising, Trump destroyed the rental assistance that used to be available - Many shelters & food banks have closed, & there's nowhere for anyone to turn, sadly..",
